cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dspk in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "dspk: multi-channel signal processing on any GPU or the CPU"
abstract: >-
  Multi-channel signal processing written once in CubeCL and run on any GPU (wgpu: Vulkan, Metal,
  DirectX 12; CUDA; ROCm / HIP) or the CPU, with the device chosen at run time: filters,
  resampling, spatial references, linear algebra, statistics, pipelines as data, and spike sorters
  (Kilosort4, EMUsort, MountainSort 5, SpyKING CIRCUS 2, Tridesclous 2) on the device.
authors:
  - given-names: Jesus
    family-names: Penaloza Aponte
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5903-2291"
repository-code: "https://github.com/neuro-kitchen/dsp-kitchen"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.4
date-released: "2026-10-29"
keywords:
  - signal processing
  - GPU
  - CubeCL
  - electrophysiology
  - spike sorting
  - Rust
  - Python
